# A mixin's function called through one includer's name (`A.get(x)`) with a value that can be another includer (B)
# passes the checker and runs A's copy on the B: this prints "get from A" twice (Ruby's x.get would say B).
# In sakelib/rails/actionpack/action_dispatch/middleware/session/cookie_store.sake the same shape,
# `Cookies::SignedKeyRotatingCookieJar.[](jar, key)` with jar = signed_or_encrypted(...) (Signed | Encrypted jar),
# checked clean and failed at run time with "TypeError: argument 1 must be ActionDispatch::Cookies::
# SignedKeyRotatingCookieJar, got ActionDispatch::Cookies::EncryptedKeyRotatingCookieJar" once the encrypted jar was
# the session's (secret_key_base set). (With a field reader in get, this small program is rejected by the checker:
# "A.v: argument 1 must be A, but can be B", so the jar's case escapes through something else in the chain.)
# Either `A.get(a_or_b)` should be rejected, or it should dispatch as `Jar.get(x)` does.
module Jar
  def name(j) = raise(NotImplementedError)
  def get(j) = "get from #{name(j)}"
end
class A
  attr_reader v
  include Jar
  def name(a) = "A"
end
class B
  attr_reader v
  include Jar
  def name(b) = "B"
end
def pick(flag) = flag ? A.new(1) : B.new(2)
puts A.get(pick(true))
puts A.get(pick(false))   # "get from A"; Ruby: "get from B"
